  "lastAssistantText": "**Fix applied.** Here's the change:\n\n**File:** `index.html`, line 739\n\n**Bug:** When a false-start occurred, `startTrial()` was called twice:\n1. First call (from the initial false-start detection) \u2192 `currentTrial++`\n2. Second call (from the retry handler) \u2192 `currentTrial++` again\n\nThis meant the trial counter advanced past the current trial, and that trial was never recorded.\n\n**Fix:** Added `currentTrial--;` in the false-start retry handler, right before calling `startTrial()`:\n\n```javascript\nplayArea.onclick = () => {\n    playArea.onclick = handleClick;\n    currentTrial--;  // Undo the increment so the same trial replays\n    startTrial();\n};\n```\n\n**Result:** The `currentTrial` value is decremented back to its original value, then `startTrial()` increments it again \u2014 so the same trial number is replayed. After exactly 5 valid reaction measurements, `times.length === 5` and the results summary will correctly show 5 rows, regardless of how many false starts occurred.",
  "workflowInstructions": "rtfm-supervised-plan.json; run-rtfm-supervised-control-v2.py",
