    "feedback": [
      {
        "number": 1,
        "id": "feedback-1-rtfm-qwen-01",
        "message": "DEFECT: False-start retry skips the trial instead of retrying it.\n\nEvidence (behavioral test run against .observed/current/index.html, hash 0821df522caa98a61d6c58d988145b7828c3002c9f4e86e1e8cb34d306011330 verified against the immutable artifact path in .observed/state.json):\n\nSetup: minimal DOM stub driving the real IIFE handlers. One false start, then normal play.\n\nResult: only 4 trial rows appear in the results summary instead of 5. A baseline run with no false start correctly records 5 trials.\n\nRoot cause: In startTrial(), currentTrial is incremented at the top. The false-start branch (phase waiting) sets playArea.onclick to a retry closure that calls startTrial() again, which increments currentTrial a second time. So tapping to retry a false-started trial advances to the next trial and the original trial is never recorded. The UI text literally says \"Tap to retry this trial\", but the behavior skips it.\n\nExpected outcome: A false-start retry must replay the SAME trial number, so all 5 trials are eventually recorded and the summary always contains 5 rows. The game should only finish after 5 valid reaction measurements, regardless of how many false starts occurred.\n\nPlease fix the false-start retry so it does not advance the trial counter (retry the same trial). Preserve all other verified-good behavior (random wait 1500-4500ms, five trials, results summary with avg/best/worst, category badges).\n",
        "reason": "verified behavioral defect: false-start retry advances the trial counter, so one false start yields only 4 of 5 recorded trials and the summary ends early; the app's own UI says 'retry this trial'. Evidence in .scratch/test_falsestart.mjs and test_baseline.mjs.",
